   "text": "The IDG FAULT light comes on if the oil outlet overheats above 180 °C or the oil pressure is low; it goes off when the IDG is disconnected.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-24-20",
     "page": "P 3/22",
     "pdf": 1466
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Pressing the IDG pb-sw disconnects the IDG from its driveshaft, and only maintenance personnel can reconnect it. Disconnect only with the engine running or windmilling. An automatic thermal disconnection occurs at 200 °C.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-24-20",
     "page": "P 3/22",
     "pdf": 1466
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "GEN 1 and 2 have priority over the APU generator. The APU generator can supply the entire network.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-24-10-30-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1446
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In flight, the APU backs up the electrical system. APU starting is permitted throughout the normal flight envelope.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-49-10-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 2570
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "ETOPS flights, engine or IDG failure: start the APU and use the APU electrical channel.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
     "page": "P 2/4",
     "pdf": 4589
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "ETOPS flights, one IDG failed: a diversion is required in the case of blue hydraulic circuit low level, low pressure or overheat, APU no start, APU or APU generator inoperative, or a second IDG failure.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "PRO-SPO-40-40",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 4586
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
